t 3.6 points and the lead went from -1.4 to -5.1, so White was clearly ahead. This was the first real gap of the game, and Opus 5.5 held it for a long stretch."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "F6 lost 9.8 points and turned a game White was leading into one Black led, from -3.3 to +6.5. It was Opus 5.5's biggest single loss before the wild middle game."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "The 8k's D5 lost 12.8 points, the worst move of Black's game. It filled in row 5 and sent the lead from +12.4 to -0.3, giving a won position straight back."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "F4 lost 10.9 points, the worst move of Opus 5.5's game. The lead went from -0.3 to +10.6, so Black took back everything that D5 had handed over."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "F7 lost 8.6 points and moved the lead from +2.9 to +11.5. After this the swings stopped and Black stayed ahead by 10 to 16 points until the end."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The only programs run were libs.py (groups and liberties of a pasted board) and count.py (area count of a pasted board), both of which just analyze the current position, plus cat/grep/tail of notes and a Python edit that appends the game log to games.md and CLAUDE.md. Nothing loops over candidate moves or plays out continuations.", "stop": false}}